DOLE Undersecretary Warren M. Miclat: And then sa case ng ILS naman po increase, ang NCMB naman po ay decrease dahil sa non-approval ng proposed additional ICT requirements

3889
04:47:06,350 --> 04:47:16,450
DOLE Undersecretary Warren M. Miclat: which is under the maintenance and other operating expenses and capital outlay at hindi rin po kami nabigyan sa NCMB ng proposed funding for the acquisition of ICT.

3890
04:47:16,470 --> 04:47:30,750
DOLE Undersecretary Warren M. Miclat: For the NLRC po, yung net decrease naman ay due to the following retirement of five commissioners with cotermius employees, non-approval ng proposed additional ICT requirements,

3891
04:47:31,410 --> 04:47:37,110
DOLE Undersecretary Warren M. Miclat: non-approval din ng proposed replacement ng fully depreciated motor vehicles.

3892
04:47:37,110 --> 04:47:42,150
DOLE Undersecretary Warren M. Miclat: Sa case ng NWPC, it's an increase. PRC is an increase.

3893
04:47:42,150 --> 04:47:55,390
DOLE Undersecretary Warren M. Miclat: TESDA is a decrease. In terms of MOE, it's a substantial reduction in the provisions of the implementation of the program such as the special training for employment program or STEP,

3894
04:47:55,810 --> 04:48:07,430
DOLE Undersecretary Warren M. Miclat: training for work scholarship program or TWSP, and lifelong employability and advancement program, micro-credentials for near-hires, in-service workers in the future workforce.

3895
04:48:07,430 --> 04:48:11,410
DOLE Undersecretary Warren M. Miclat: And also a reduction in their foreign-assisted project.

3896
04:48:12,150 --> 04:48:19,210
DOLE Undersecretary Warren M. Miclat: Particularly the supporting innovation in the Philippine Technical and Vocational Education and Training System or SIPTIVETS.

3897
04:48:19,610 --> 04:48:24,390
DOLE Undersecretary Warren M. Miclat: And capital outlay, no provision for their ICT and vehicle as well.

3898
04:48:25,190 --> 04:48:26,010
DOLE Undersecretary Warren M. Miclat: Thanks po.

3899
04:48:26,510 --> 04:48:32,950
Rep. Antonino B. Roman III: So, in particular, yung computerization, paano ito nakakapekto sa trabaho ng DOLE?

3900
04:48:34,410 --> 04:48:39,630
DOLE Undersecretary Warren M. Miclat: Yung sa computerization naman po, sa 2026 may budget naman po kami.

3901
04:48:41,010 --> 04:48:50,730
DOLE Undersecretary Warren M. Miclat: Ang hindi na lang po na-provide for next year, yung mga capital outlay na pambili ng mga hardware like computers, kasi meron na po provided for 2026.

3902
04:48:50,730 --> 04:49:01,110
DOLE Undersecretary Warren M. Miclat: At may mga natira pa po na 2025 na continuing po na this year na dapat na rin po naming maubos, pambili rin po ng mga hardware components such as desktop, laptop, computers.

3903
04:49:01,570 --> 04:49:04,510
DOLE Undersecretary Warren M. Miclat: At ito po ay mga nakapila na po for the procurement process po.

3904
04:49:05,770 --> 04:49:09,130
Rep. Antonino B. Roman III: Mr. Secretary, kanina yung tinanong ni Kong Jolo.

3905
04:49:09,130 --> 04:49:18,630
Rep. Antonino B. Roman III: Yung programa na naisip ninyo, yung NALJ or National Academy of Labor Justice at saka yung Labor Attorney's Office.

3906
04:49:19,390 --> 04:49:27,750
Rep. Antonino B. Roman III: Ito ho ba kasama na mga programang isinumiti nyo pero hindi na pondohan?

3907
04:49:28,590 --> 04:49:29,750
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Kasama po yan.

3908
04:49:29,750 --> 04:49:37,750
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: In fact, we wrote a separate letter to the Speaker of the House, the members of...

3909
04:49:39,130 --> 04:49:43,310
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: And committees and pretty soon with the Senate President himself.

3910
04:49:43,310 --> 04:49:47,210
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: So, naniniwala po kami na kailangan ito. Ano lang naman po?

3911
04:49:48,630 --> 04:49:51,650
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: 50 million plus 75 million.

3912
04:49:52,190 --> 04:49:56,490
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: 125 million po to address the...

3913
04:49:56,490 --> 04:50:06,790
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: One, to address the needs of the workers in Labor Attorney's Office para may free legal assistance sila nationwide to hire 64 lawyers.

3914
04:50:06,790 --> 04:50:07,790
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: And then yung pangalawa...

3915
04:50:09,130 --> 04:50:18,790
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Para magkaroon tayo ng isang academy na magte-training sa mga mediators, conciliators, labor arbiters, etc., etc.

3916
04:50:19,070 --> 04:50:20,610
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: And continuing education na rin po.

3917
04:50:20,610 --> 04:50:29,010
Rep. Antonino B. Roman III: Ito yung gap na nakita nyo sa loob ng tatlong buwan magmula nung itinalaga kayo na sekretary ng DOLE.

3918
04:50:29,090 --> 04:50:30,790
Rep. Antonino B. Roman III: Ito yung gap na gusto nyong punan.

3919
04:50:31,770 --> 04:50:35,610
Rep. Antonino B. Roman III: Yung training sa mga quasi-judicial officers. Tama po ba?

3920
04:50:35,890 --> 04:50:37,030
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Opo, in the short term.

3921
04:50:37,270 --> 04:50:38,610
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: At marami pa po rin tayong...

3922
04:50:39,130 --> 04:50:43,990
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Kagaya po ang nasabi ko kanina, siguro ad hoc na lang po yun.

3923
04:50:45,250 --> 04:50:52,810
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Tatag po tayo ng isang Maritime Labor Affairs Office para naman po mag-comply sa International Labor Organization.

3924
04:50:54,270 --> 04:50:56,890
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: At para matulungan din yung ating mga tripulante.

3925
04:50:57,670 --> 04:51:03,030
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Hindi lang yung nasa laot kung hindi yung mga nagsisiman pa rito, etc., etc.

3926
04:51:03,610 --> 04:51:08,690
Rep. Antonino B. Roman III: Yung sa hinihingi nyo po na pondo para sa NALJ na lang para may click.

3927
04:51:09,130 --> 04:51:12,970
Rep. Antonino B. Roman III: Na 50 million. Ano po yung batayan o basis ng 50 million?

3928
04:51:12,970 --> 04:51:21,750
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Meron po kaming makapal na dokumento rito para dun sa 83 pages po ito.

3929
04:51:22,110 --> 04:51:35,770
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Para dun lang po to operationalize this proposal, it would require a retooling of the existing ILS.

3930
04:51:35,770 --> 04:51:37,090
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: I have to be frank.

3931
04:51:37,650 --> 04:51:38,870
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Institute of Labor.

3932
04:51:38,870 --> 04:51:44,290
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: For studies, it would require the creation of a governing board.

3933
04:51:44,750 --> 04:51:53,450
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: It would require the creation of an office of a chancellor, a better library and research development program,

3934
04:51:54,170 --> 04:52:01,430
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: as well as pursue the two pillars I mentioned a while ago, labor justice, education, professional formation.

3935
04:52:01,650 --> 04:52:03,110
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: This is a continuing education.

3936
04:52:03,110 --> 04:52:08,470
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: And then, pillar two is labor justice policy, research and knowledge development,

3937
04:52:08,870 --> 04:52:09,970
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: which is the focus of the ILS.

3938
04:52:09,970 --> 04:52:11,590
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Eventually, produce publications.

3939
04:52:12,050 --> 04:52:15,930
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Kung makikita nyo po, your honor, napakagaling ng Bureau of Internal Revenue,

3940
04:52:16,610 --> 04:52:22,150
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: yung kanilang mga issuances, regulations, number, blah, ganun po.

3941
04:52:23,010 --> 04:52:27,290
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Sa amin po, medyo nalilito na rin ako na dun sa numbering pa lang.

3942
04:52:27,870 --> 04:52:30,110
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: So, we hope to codify all of this.

3943
04:52:30,110 --> 04:52:36,510
Rep. Antonino B. Roman III: So, parang silang merong database sa mga precedents na pwedeng pagbatayan

3944
04:52:36,510 --> 04:52:41,250
Rep. Antonino B. Roman III: para consistent po yung paglabas sa mga desisyon at saka mga rulings,

3945
04:52:41,330 --> 04:52:46,510
Rep. Antonino B. Roman III: dahil meron silang parang, pwede silang sumangguni dun sa database na yun.

3946
04:52:46,830 --> 04:52:52,070
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Gusto rin namin po magkaroon ng ISCRA para sa NLRC.

3947
04:52:52,990 --> 04:52:56,250
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Gusto rin namin magkaroon ng ISCRA para sa mga labor arbiters.

3948
04:52:56,250 --> 04:53:05,450
Rep. Antonino B. Roman III: Ngayon po, sa proposed NEP for 2027, binanggit po ni Undersecretary kanina na tumaas po yung budget para sa ILS.

3949
04:53:06,010 --> 04:53:06,490
Rep. Antonino B. Roman III: Now, binanggit po yung budget para sa ILS.

3950
04:53:06,490 --> 04:53:11,950
Rep. Antonino B. Roman III: So, binanggit po yung NALJ. Yan po ang papalit sa ILS.

3951
04:53:12,550 --> 04:53:17,390
Rep. Antonino B. Roman III: Yung karagdagang pondo na mapupunta sa, at yung pondong nilaan para sa ILS, I would assume,

3952
04:53:18,430 --> 04:53:21,910
Rep. Antonino B. Roman III: the NALJ will take over. Tama po ba?

3953
04:53:22,310 --> 04:53:29,170
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Correct. But the present increase in the NEP of the ILS is just for the ILS per se.

3954
04:53:29,530 --> 04:53:29,810
Rep. Antonino B. Roman III: Okay.

3955
04:53:29,810 --> 04:53:35,810
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Hindi pa po nakapatong dun yung NALJ because NALJ would require,

3956
04:53:35,810 --> 04:53:45,470
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: itong 50 million na ito, ma-itemize naman po ito, would require the additional facilities such as a digital library

3957
04:53:45,470 --> 04:54:00,150
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: and perhaps a modest courtroom, parang moot court, na kung saan pwedeng mag-practice yung mga nag-a-apply na NLRC commissioner or labor arbiters.

3958
04:54:00,270 --> 04:54:03,210
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Ganon din po yung mga estudyante nating fourth year sa law school.

3959
04:54:03,210 --> 04:54:05,750
Rep. Antonino B. Roman III: Yung detalye po na yan, yung hawak nyo,

3960
04:54:05,810 --> 04:54:07,010
Rep. Antonino B. Roman III: na-submitin na po sa committee.

3961
04:54:09,010 --> 04:54:13,310
Rep. Antonino B. Roman III: Kasi yan po yung parang justification for the 50 million for the NALJ.

3962
04:54:13,330 --> 04:54:15,130
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Yes, we can submit this, Your Honor, today.

3963
04:54:15,150 --> 04:54:15,750
Rep. Antonino B. Roman III: Kung maaari po.

3964
04:54:15,910 --> 04:54:22,770
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Opo. Although this is my copy, kung tatanggapin nyo po, may mga notes, notes lang ako. May mga sulat lang ako eh.

3965
04:54:23,050 --> 04:54:33,610
Rep. Antonino B. Roman III: And then, pangalawa po, same request for the Labor Attorney's Office, 75 million, some justification for, the justification for that, the computation.

3966
04:54:33,610 --> 04:54:34,610
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Ipipigay ko na po ngayon.

3967
04:54:34,610 --> 04:54:43,410
Rep. Antonino B. Roman III: Dahil doon po sa Labor Attorney's Office yung sinasabi nyo, kailangan ng 64 na labor arbiters, 32 legal officers.

3968
04:54:43,410 --> 04:54:47,410
Rep. Antonino B. Roman III: Pag nakikita po akong ganyang eksaktong detalye, ang tanong ko, bakit ganun na numero?

3969
04:54:47,410 --> 04:54:51,410
Rep. Antonino B. Roman III: So, kung meron po kayong justification, kung maaari po isumiti sa committee.

3970
04:54:51,410 --> 04:55:01,410
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Ito po yan, Your Honor. Ibibigay ko na po ngayon yung, meron naman kaming digital file nito, pero marami na po akong sulat-sulat dito.

3971
04:55:01,410 --> 04:55:09,410
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Kung tatanggapin nyo po ito, eh, ibibigay ko po. Wala po ako ditong mga drawing-drawing, Your Honor. Malinis po ito.

3972
04:55:10,170 --> 04:55:19,670
Rep. Antonino B. Roman III: Ngayon, yung ano po, yung sa Labor Attorney's Office, ang pagkakalam ko po, yung Public Attorney's Office, yan na po yung mandato eh.

3973
04:55:20,110 --> 04:55:29,510
Rep. Antonino B. Roman III: Natulungan yung mga indigent litigants. Hindi po sapat yung trabaho na ginagawa ng pao na kinakailangan po ng Labor Attorney's Office?

3974
04:55:29,530 --> 04:55:31,250
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Ah, nandun po sa...

3975
04:55:31,250 --> 04:55:34,330
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Naipasa ko na eh. Nangirapan na akong kabulin si...

3976
04:55:34,330 --> 04:55:35,690
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Ibibigay na kay Chairman.

3977
04:55:36,150 --> 04:55:44,330
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Meron po kaming datos doon na yung workload ng PAO ay halos nakatutok sa mga criminal cases sa probinsya.

3978
04:55:44,590 --> 04:55:52,190
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: May mga civil cases din at kakaunti po ang nabibigyan ng konsiderasyon sa mga labor arbiters.

3979
04:55:52,690 --> 04:55:57,550
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Lalong-lalo na yung mga nakabase po sa Metro Manila at yung mga regional centers natin.

3980
04:55:57,550 --> 04:56:00,910
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: So, meron po ditong justification, yung percentage ng...

3981
04:56:00,910 --> 04:56:06,030
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: trabaho ng Public Attorney's Office patungkol po doon sa kanilang workload.

3982
04:56:06,570 --> 04:56:10,010
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Na ang bulk po ay yung talagang pampiskal.

3983
04:56:10,670 --> 04:56:13,150
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Ang workload po ay yung mga pang-RTC.

3984
04:56:13,670 --> 04:56:19,330
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: So, dito po sa arbitration, sa conciliation, ay halos wala po.

3985
04:56:19,810 --> 04:56:20,750
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Meron pa isa-isa.

3986
04:56:21,430 --> 04:56:27,870
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Lalong-lalo na po sa pangkaraniwang kasong dinudulog po sa amin.

3987
04:56:27,870 --> 04:56:29,870
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: So, yun po ay...

3988
04:56:29,870 --> 04:56:35,830
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Yung po ang nagsulong para sa tanggapan na itulak itong mungkahing ito.

3989
04:56:35,930 --> 04:56:41,890
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: At nandun po lahat ng data na hindi ko na po masight ngayon kasi napilitan akong iabot na kay Chairman.

3990
04:56:42,330 --> 04:56:43,310
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Nandun po sa kanya.

3991
04:56:43,550 --> 04:56:50,750
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Actually, Mr. Secretary, I was instructing the Secretariat na if amenable naman si Rep. Tony Roman

3992
04:56:50,750 --> 04:56:56,290
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: after the once-a-day copies have been furnished, we'll furnish a copy to Rep. Tony Roman.

3993
04:56:58,630 --> 04:56:59,210
Rep. Antonino B. Roman III: And then...

3994
04:56:59,870 --> 04:57:10,350
Rep. Antonino B. Roman III: Kung dalawang programa na gusto nyo na karagdaga na pondo, yung NALJ at at yung Legal Labor Attorney's Office,

3995
04:57:10,530 --> 04:57:11,710
Rep. Antonino B. Roman III: ito po ba magkaugnay?

3996
04:57:12,610 --> 04:57:17,870
Rep. Antonino B. Roman III: Kailangan package deal na magkasama o may ding paghiwalay yan?

3997
04:57:18,430 --> 04:57:20,210
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Magkahiwalay po yan, but they work together.

3998
04:57:20,390 --> 04:57:21,370
Rep. Antonino B. Roman III: Very complimentary po.

3999
04:57:21,430 --> 04:57:23,490
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Opo, complimentary sila.

4000
04:57:23,490 --> 04:57:28,430
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: And it's very timely, Your Honor, kasi po ngayon darating na 2027,

4001
04:57:28,430 --> 04:57:37,910
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: ang Pilipinas po ang mamumuno ng International Labor Council sa ILO sa Geneva.

4002
04:57:38,890 --> 04:57:48,430
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: So, nais po nating ipakita sa ibang bansa na meron tayong ganitong mga tanggapan

4003
04:57:48,430 --> 04:57:52,890
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: na talagang tumutugon sa pangangailangan ng ating manggagawa,

4004
04:57:53,030 --> 04:57:56,770
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: including that National Academy for Labor Justice, which is a first.

4005
04:57:57,310 --> 04:57:57,770
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Marami po tayong mga...

4006
04:57:58,430 --> 04:58:04,350
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Mga kabataang Pilipino na nag-aaral ng abugasya, first year, second year,

4007
04:58:04,810 --> 04:58:07,050
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: hindi pa nila alam pag sila ay...

4008
04:58:07,050 --> 04:58:10,630
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Kasi pagkakaiba po sa medical school, first year, second year,

4009
04:58:10,730 --> 04:58:16,050
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: alam mo na kung ikaw ay magiging surgeon kung gusto mong mag-specialize.

4010
04:58:16,050 --> 04:58:24,690
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: So, ito po ay magbubukas ng pinto para sa mga law students na ay maganda pala ang labor justice.

4011
04:58:25,350 --> 04:58:27,330
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Dito tayo mag-specialize.

4012
04:58:28,430 --> 04:58:34,130
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: O gaya ngayon, pag-graduate mo ng law school, parang general practitioner ka na sa medisina, ganun din.

4013
04:58:34,710 --> 04:58:40,930
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: So, natatangi po ito, hindi sa pagbubuhat ng sariling bangko, kasi itong dalawang ito, first time.

4014
04:58:42,070 --> 04:58:43,570
Rep. Antonino B. Roman III: Maraming salamat.

4015
04:58:43,570 --> 04:58:45,550
Rep. Antonino B. Roman III: Now to Secretary Benitez.

4016
04:58:46,230 --> 04:58:49,890
Rep. Antonino B. Roman III: May napapansin ko, madalang po ipa nagtatanong sa kanya.

4017
04:58:50,650 --> 04:58:52,090
Rep. Antonino B. Roman III: Kaya magtatanong ako sa kanya.

4018
04:58:52,910 --> 04:58:53,470
Rep. Antonino B. Roman III: Same question.

4019
04:58:53,470 --> 04:58:53,710
Rep. Antonino B. Roman III: Sige, sir.

4020
04:58:54,330 --> 04:58:58,090
Rep. Antonino B. Roman III: Yung nakita niyo po yung Neptune for 2027, meron mo bang aspeto doon?

4021
04:58:58,430 --> 04:59:01,110
Rep. Antonino B. Roman III: Na napailing kayo at halos maluha.

4022
04:59:02,470 --> 04:59:03,530
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: Marami rin po.

4023
04:59:03,990 --> 04:59:04,850
Rep. Antonino B. Roman III: Ano po yung mga yun?

4024
04:59:05,430 --> 04:59:07,030
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: Siguro, unahin ko na lang.

4025
04:59:07,250 --> 04:59:19,710
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: We made a request for more positions, particularly in the field, to help us roll out and implement our programs with greater efficiency.

4026
04:59:20,450 --> 04:59:24,710
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: We also made a greater request, sir, for capital outlay.

4027
04:59:24,710 --> 04:59:26,750
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: Wala pong capital outlay.

4028
04:59:26,750 --> 04:59:34,370
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: Pero yung talagang naluluha ako, siguro, ay ang pagliit po ng aming scholarship budget.

4029
04:59:35,990 --> 04:59:49,610
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: Which is also how I ended my presentation earlier, with a request that at the very least, in order to ensure that the expansion of the education reform and its implementation in accordance with the NAD plan,

4030
04:59:49,610 --> 04:59:56,650
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: at the very least sana, maging equal sa GAA ng 2026, ang budget po ng test.

4031
04:59:56,750 --> 04:59:57,890
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: Sa 2027.

4032
04:59:58,590 --> 04:59:59,990
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: If you can...

4033
05:00:00,000 --> 05:00:08,260
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: Notice, ang pinakamalaki pong hiningi namin sa aming, hindi ho kasi wish list yun eh, kagaya ng sinabi ni Kong Jolo kanina,

4034
05:00:08,780 --> 05:00:15,120
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: eh yung wish list ho namin eh, an additional 20 billion na marahil naman eh hindi mabibigay, no.

4035
05:00:15,200 --> 05:00:17,160
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: Nasabi na ho sa amin ni Kong Jila yan.

4036
05:00:18,500 --> 05:00:24,420
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: But the biggest portion, sir, is actually in the universal access to quality tertiary education.

4037
05:00:24,420 --> 05:00:29,420
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: We are requesting an additional 2.4 billion for our diploma programs nationwide,

4038
05:00:30,260 --> 05:00:35,420
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: so that as we expand towards higher level training with greater skill and greater productivity,

4039
05:00:36,680 --> 05:00:43,760
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: ay masuportahan din po namin ng budget namin ang kapipirima lang po na amendment to the UACTA law last week.

4040
05:00:44,360 --> 05:00:50,840
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: So the request is really to make sure that at the very least,

4041
05:00:50,840 --> 05:00:53,840
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: our budget for 2027 is more or less equivalent,

4042
