4411
05:23:00,370 --> 05:23:06,370
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: So next will be on the majority side, Rep. Anna York Bondok.

4412
05:23:06,370 --> 05:23:09,370
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Thank you so much, Mr. Chair.

4413
05:23:09,370 --> 05:23:13,370
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: And first of all, I'd like to congratulate our new Secretary of State,

4414
05:23:13,370 --> 05:23:15,370
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: our new Secretary of Labor.

4415
05:23:15,370 --> 05:23:18,370
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: One of the best senators and pinak-mabayit din po.

4416
05:23:18,370 --> 05:23:22,370
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: And we are very happy to have him now at the DOLE.

4417
05:23:22,370 --> 05:23:29,370
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: So my first question is, we are very worried about children and the internet.

4418
05:23:29,370 --> 05:23:38,370
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: And especially its relationship po to violence and other issues regarding children's mental health.

4419
05:23:38,370 --> 05:23:41,370
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Can you tell us more about Labor Advisory No. 12?

4420
05:23:41,370 --> 05:23:43,370
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: And child influencers.

4421
05:23:43,370 --> 05:23:46,370
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Worse, hindi lang sila nagkoconsume sa internet.

4422
05:23:46,370 --> 05:23:49,370
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: E sila pa po yung nagpe-perform sa internet.

4423
05:23:49,370 --> 05:23:52,370
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: I'm just only hoping that it is safe.

4424
05:23:52,370 --> 05:23:57,370
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Yung ginagawa po nila ay hindi po exploitation ng children.

4425
05:23:57,370 --> 05:23:59,370
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: In fact, by their own parents.

4426
05:23:59,370 --> 05:24:01,370
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Kasi kumikita po ito.

4427
05:24:01,370 --> 05:24:04,370
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Nagulat po ako na yung kaklase daw ng anak ko, so ni grade 9.

4428
05:24:04,370 --> 05:24:06,370
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: A makeup influencer na raw.

4429
05:24:06,370 --> 05:24:08,370
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: At marami na raw kinikita.

4430
05:24:08,370 --> 05:24:11,370
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: So can you let us know what is the DOLE's stand on this?

4431
05:24:11,370 --> 05:24:14,370
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: And what are you doing po to protect our children

4432
05:24:14,370 --> 05:24:19,370
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: from not only consuming but performing internet activities?

4433
05:24:19,370 --> 05:24:22,370
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Ang salamat po, Congresswoman.

4434
05:24:22,370 --> 05:24:28,370
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: I-issue lang po namin hindi katagalan yung Advisory No. 12.

4435
05:24:28,370 --> 05:24:35,370
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: At ang nilalaman po nito ay para bigyan din at laman yung protection para sa ating mga kabataan below 15.

4436
05:24:35,370 --> 05:24:37,370
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Dalawa po ang aspeto nito.

4437
05:24:37,370 --> 05:24:39,370
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Yung nagtatrabaho po na kontrolado ng magulang.

4438
05:24:39,370 --> 05:24:40,370
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: At yung nagtatrabaho po

4439
05:24:40,370 --> 05:24:43,370
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: At yung nagtatrabaho po kontrolado ng employer.

4440
05:24:43,370 --> 05:24:51,370
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Sa dalawang branch po ay amin po sinisigurado na ang kabataang Pilipino ay hindi ma-exploit.

4441
05:24:51,370 --> 05:24:56,370
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Hindi magtatrabaho ng between 10 to 6 ng madaling araw.

4442
05:24:56,370 --> 05:25:02,370
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: At mangangailangan po ng permit kung ito ay nagtatrabaho sa isang employer.

4443
05:25:02,370 --> 05:25:09,370
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: At mangangailangan din po na siguraduhin yung kikitain niya 20% lang ang mapupunta po sa pamilya.

4444
05:25:09,370 --> 05:25:15,370
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: At yung 80% ay mapupunta sa kanyang pag-aaral, sa kanyang well-being, sa kanyang kalusugan.

4445
05:25:15,370 --> 05:25:19,370
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Nang sa ganun po hindi po ma-exploit yung kabataang Pilipino.

4446
05:25:19,370 --> 05:25:22,370
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Lalawang lalo na yung pumapasok sa dalawang uri po yan.

4447
05:25:22,370 --> 05:25:24,370
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Entertainment yung isa.

4448
05:25:24,370 --> 05:25:29,370
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: At yung isa po ay talagang nagsusuporta doon sa mga advertisements, etc., etc.

4449
05:25:29,370 --> 05:25:31,370
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Lumalabas sa mga television shows.

4450
05:25:31,370 --> 05:25:34,370
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: At makikita natin pinagahanap buhay na ng maaga.

4451
05:25:34,370 --> 05:25:35,370
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Uulitin ko po ito.

4452
05:25:35,370 --> 05:25:38,370
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Ang layunin po nito ay tumupad sa napakaraming ILO commitment.

4453
05:25:38,370 --> 05:25:42,370
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Ng Pilipinas na huwag ma-exploit ang kabataang Pilipino.

4454
05:25:42,370 --> 05:25:44,370
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Kabilang na rin po dito yung mga nagtatrabaho.

4455
05:25:44,370 --> 05:25:49,370
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Di umano sa ilang ulat na nagtatrabaho sa minahan.

4456
05:25:49,370 --> 05:25:53,370
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Nagtatrabaho sa palengke ng pinagbubuhat.

4457
05:25:53,370 --> 05:25:56,370
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Yan po ay hindi natin kinakontinence.

4458
05:25:56,370 --> 05:26:04,370
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Subalit sa internet ay napakalaki pong puhang ang nangyayari dahil sa bahay lang po ito.

4459
05:26:04,370 --> 05:26:06,370
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Iba po yung nasa internet.

4460
05:26:06,370 --> 05:26:07,370
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Yes.

4461
05:26:07,370 --> 05:26:09,370
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: So ito pong guidelines na nilabas namin.

4462
05:26:09,370 --> 05:26:11,370
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Well disseminated na ito.

4463
05:26:11,370 --> 05:26:21,370
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: At sana po ay magkaroon ng hindi lamang katuparan yung ninanais ng International Labour Organization.

4464
05:26:21,370 --> 05:26:23,370
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Para ma-prevent din.

4465
05:26:23,370 --> 05:26:26,370
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: May alam nga ako, two years old pa lang eh.

4466
05:26:26,370 --> 05:26:34,370
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Lumalabas na sa Facebook at sa ibang platforms.

4467
05:26:34,370 --> 05:26:35,370
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: So yun po yung nilalaman.

4468
05:26:35,370 --> 05:26:45,370
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: And we can provide your honor a copy of that Labor Advisory Number 12.

4469
05:26:45,370 --> 05:26:50,370
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: I would like to congratulate you po on this groundbreaking advisory.

4470
05:26:50,370 --> 05:26:53,370
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Lalo na po bago-bago pa lang pero nakagawa na po.

4471
05:26:53,370 --> 05:26:58,370
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: My question is, how are you enforcing this?

4472
05:26:58,370 --> 05:27:02,370
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Unang-una po yung wide dissemination ng Labor Advisory.

4473
05:27:02,370 --> 05:27:03,370
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Hindi.

4474
05:27:03,370 --> 05:27:06,370
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Nakontak niyo po ba yung matataasang views sa FB?

4475
05:27:06,370 --> 05:27:07,370
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: I don't know.

4476
05:27:07,370 --> 05:27:08,370
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Opo.

4477
05:27:08,370 --> 05:27:11,370
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Sa ngayon po, dahil bago-bago pa lang po yan,

4478
05:27:11,370 --> 05:27:17,370
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: yung aming po ang Bureau of Local Employment ang nakatalagang mag-monitor niyan.

4479
05:27:17,370 --> 05:27:20,370
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Lalong-lalo na yung nasa entertainment industry.

4480
05:27:20,370 --> 05:27:24,370
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Ang sinasabi ko po dito, yung lumalabas sa mga TV shows.

4481
05:27:24,370 --> 05:27:28,720
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Lahat po yan ay namamonitor.

4482
05:27:28,720 --> 05:27:33,720
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: So ito pong iba, siguro po yung BLE namin ay sa number of followers.

4483
05:27:33,720 --> 05:27:36,720
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Merong gustong idagdag si Secreyes?

4484
05:27:36,720 --> 05:27:43,280
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Can you share any data like how many child influencers na po ang nasa internet?

4485
05:27:43,280 --> 05:27:45,280
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: And what is the average age?

4486
05:27:45,280 --> 05:27:48,280
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Kasi mga infants pa yung iba eh.

4487
05:27:48,280 --> 05:27:50,280
DOLE Assistant Secretary Amuerfina R. Reyes: If I may po, ma'am.

4488
05:27:50,280 --> 05:27:54,280
DOLE Assistant Secretary Amuerfina R. Reyes: Well, yung tanong niyo po pa dina, what do we do?

4489
05:27:54,280 --> 05:28:00,280
DOLE Assistant Secretary Amuerfina R. Reyes: Naglabas na po si Sec ng Labor Advisory 12 na okay na po yun.

4490
05:28:00,280 --> 05:28:03,280
DOLE Assistant Secretary Amuerfina R. Reyes: But of course, the monitoring is one of the challenges.

4491
05:28:03,280 --> 05:28:07,280
DOLE Assistant Secretary Amuerfina R. Reyes: But meron din ho kaming makabata hotline na tinatawag.

4492
05:28:07,280 --> 05:28:14,280
DOLE Assistant Secretary Amuerfina R. Reyes: Na pwede ho kasing mag-report doon sa hotline na yun yung ating mga kababayan.

4493
05:28:14,280 --> 05:28:18,280
DOLE Assistant Secretary Amuerfina R. Reyes: But meron din ho mga reports galing din ho sa ating mga regional offices.

4494
05:28:18,280 --> 05:28:26,280
DOLE Assistant Secretary Amuerfina R. Reyes: Nagko-conduct po sila ng mga validation report at saka interview sa blogger at saka doon sa parents nung bata.

4495
05:28:26,280 --> 05:28:30,280
DOLE Assistant Secretary Amuerfina R. Reyes: At tinitingnan din ho yan kung meron silang working child permit.

4496
05:28:30,280 --> 05:28:32,280
DOLE Assistant Secretary Amuerfina R. Reyes: Well, yung katotohanan po ma'am.

4497
05:28:32,280 --> 05:28:39,280
DOLE Assistant Secretary Amuerfina R. Reyes: Hindi naman lahat ho kasi ay nakakaalam na kailangan pala nila kumuha ng working child permit.

4498
05:28:39,280 --> 05:28:44,280
DOLE Assistant Secretary Amuerfina R. Reyes: Kaya yung labor advisory will serve as a guidance for them na kahit magulang,

4499
05:28:44,280 --> 05:28:50,280
DOLE Assistant Secretary Amuerfina R. Reyes: kahit na anong establishments na pwedeng gusto kumuha ng bata at magtrabaho sa bata,

4500
05:28:50,280 --> 05:28:53,280
DOLE Assistant Secretary Amuerfina R. Reyes: sisiguraduhin nilang natutupad nila yung mga requirements.

4501
05:28:53,280 --> 05:28:59,280
DOLE Assistant Secretary Amuerfina R. Reyes: Unang-una, hindi ho kailangan na mapabayaan yung well-being of children.

4502
05:28:59,280 --> 05:29:01,280
DOLE Assistant Secretary Amuerfina R. Reyes: Kahit they are being engaged in this kind of work,

4503
05:29:02,280 --> 05:29:06,280
DOLE Assistant Secretary Amuerfina R. Reyes: at meron silang work, kakondisyon ho yun doon sa working child permit.

4504
05:29:06,280 --> 05:29:08,280
DOLE Assistant Secretary Amuerfina R. Reyes: Kailangan ng bata nakakapag-aral.

4505
05:29:08,280 --> 05:29:11,280
DOLE Assistant Secretary Amuerfina R. Reyes: Hindi siya full time na nagtatrabaho.

4506
05:29:11,280 --> 05:29:15,280
DOLE Assistant Secretary Amuerfina R. Reyes: At meron din po siyang oras para siya ay makapaglaro.

4507
05:29:15,280 --> 05:29:20,280
DOLE Assistant Secretary Amuerfina R. Reyes: So ang mga regional offices po natin ma'am, ang nagmamonitor po nito.

4508
05:29:20,280 --> 05:29:25,280
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Ma'am, sana po yung mga kumpanya din po that actually pay for their ads,

4509
05:29:25,280 --> 05:29:30,280
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: they should not be allowed to employ po kids na wala pong permit and they should be fined.

4510
05:29:30,280 --> 05:29:34,280
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Kasi sila po ang kumikita na malaki, yung mga corporations.

4511
05:29:34,280 --> 05:29:39,280
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Kasama po ba yun sa advisory? I'm sorry, I didn't see a copy but I'm very interested.

4512
05:29:39,280 --> 05:29:45,280
DOLE Assistant Secretary Amuerfina R. Reyes: Even before po ng advisory, may batas na po kasi tayo diyan, as you know very well.

4513
05:29:45,280 --> 05:29:48,280
DOLE Assistant Secretary Amuerfina R. Reyes: So para po doon sa mga private companies sa formal sector,

4514
05:29:48,280 --> 05:29:53,280
DOLE Assistant Secretary Amuerfina R. Reyes: minomonitor po yan ng mga regional offices natin through our labor inspection program.

4515
05:29:53,280 --> 05:29:58,280
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Yes, ma'am. I am not referring to children like singing and dancing on stage.

4516
05:29:58,280 --> 05:30:00,000
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: But as you know,

4517
05:30:00,000 --> 05:30:04,400
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: So, P50,000 na po per mention lang po.

4518
05:30:04,700 --> 05:30:06,840
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: And these are not even for famous influencers.

4519
05:30:07,540 --> 05:30:11,380
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: So, for the kids po, they can earn P100,000, P200,000 per post.

4520
05:30:11,920 --> 05:30:15,900
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: So, sana po yung mga kumpanya would also be aware that this is a form of child labor.

4521
05:30:16,340 --> 05:30:20,580
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Sometimes we just think, andun lang sa bahay, pinifilm ni mommy, pero hindi po, trabaho yun.

4522
05:30:21,220 --> 05:30:23,080
DOLE Assistant Secretary Amuerfina R. Reyes: Opo, tama po kayo doon.

4523
05:30:23,080 --> 05:30:25,680
DOLE Assistant Secretary Amuerfina R. Reyes: Kaya nga po, pagdating naman sa mga kumpanya, ma'am,

4524
05:30:25,680 --> 05:30:30,180
DOLE Assistant Secretary Amuerfina R. Reyes: pag pumunta ang ating labor inspector, isa yan sa tinitingnan din po nila.

4525
05:30:30,380 --> 05:30:34,900
DOLE Assistant Secretary Amuerfina R. Reyes: Plus yung monitoring po natin sa mga social media, kasama din po yun.

4526
05:30:35,180 --> 05:30:37,900
DOLE Assistant Secretary Amuerfina R. Reyes: But marami pong salamat doon sa inyong recommendation.

4527
05:30:37,980 --> 05:30:40,580
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Thank you so much. Ma'am, maalaking bagay po yan.

4528
05:30:41,280 --> 05:30:44,680
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Thank you so much also for your attention to this sec, and congratulations.

4529
05:30:45,420 --> 05:30:49,500
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: I would like to react po doon sa tupad po na sinabing ayuda.

4530
05:30:50,080 --> 05:30:53,000
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Hindi po ayuda yung tupad kasi nagtatrabaho kayo.

4531
05:30:53,420 --> 05:30:55,500
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: So, this is a form of short-term employment.

4532
05:30:55,680 --> 05:31:01,940
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: So, ililinaw ko lang po na hopefully na ilinaw nyo rin po that wala pong ayuda included.

4533
05:31:02,180 --> 05:31:04,360
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Kasi our concept of ayuda is bibigyan ka lang ng pera.

4534
05:31:04,660 --> 05:31:06,200
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: But that is not the concept po.

4535
05:31:06,300 --> 05:31:09,980
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: And I think that is not what we are thinking of when we do tupad.

4536
05:31:10,400 --> 05:31:15,100
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: So, sana po, siguro what we need to strengthen po sa tupad is the monitoring.

4537
05:31:15,960 --> 05:31:19,820
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Kasi kung hindi naman po nababantayan yung mga tao, talagang upo na lang po.

4538
05:31:20,240 --> 05:31:24,720
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: And I would suggest that the percentage of the tupad be used to monitor mismo.

4539
05:31:24,720 --> 05:31:26,400
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Or to hire monitors.

4540
05:31:26,960 --> 05:31:28,880
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Or to get independent monitors.

4541
05:31:29,640 --> 05:31:31,800
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: And then, kailangan po malinaw yung deliverables.

4542
05:31:31,980 --> 05:31:33,080
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Ano bang gagawin nila?

4543
05:31:34,480 --> 05:31:37,840
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: And then, finally, you might also want to collab po.

4544
05:31:38,200 --> 05:31:44,520
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Sa amin po, yung GIP namin, they work in schools as assistant teachers for the teachers.

4545
05:31:45,100 --> 05:31:49,060
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Assistant admin for those who are not, these are new graduates.

4546
05:31:49,400 --> 05:31:52,340
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: So, assistant admin po sa mga hindi BS education.

4547
05:31:52,340 --> 05:31:53,880
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Tapos may nagtanong po.

4548
05:31:54,720 --> 05:31:58,780
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Yung mga criminology graduates, ano daw ang gagawin nila sa school?

4549
05:31:59,160 --> 05:32:03,460
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Naisip po na isang principal namin, sila po yung magbubukas ng mga bag na mga bata.

4550
05:32:04,400 --> 05:32:06,140
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: So, that was supposed to be a joke.

4551
05:32:08,200 --> 05:32:12,120
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: So, ang nagmamonitor po sa kanila, yung DepEd.

4552
05:32:12,440 --> 05:32:15,720
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: So, may monitor na hindi po sila.

4553
05:32:15,940 --> 05:32:17,400
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: So, you need to have a monitoring.

4554
05:32:18,060 --> 05:32:19,520
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: So, kailangan po talaga yan.

4555
05:32:19,520 --> 05:32:21,320
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: And then, I would like to share some.

4556
05:32:21,840 --> 05:32:22,600
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Pwede po bang?

4557
05:32:23,560 --> 05:32:24,560
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: If you could share po.

4558
05:32:24,720 --> 05:32:30,420
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: So, if you might want to publish po yung mga ginagawa ng mga tao sa Tupad para makita po nila.

4559
05:32:30,960 --> 05:32:31,980
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Para malaman.

4560
05:32:32,280 --> 05:32:35,260
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: I'd like to, meron po kaming gulayan ni Nana.

4561
05:32:35,380 --> 05:32:37,260
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: If you have a picture po, that would be very good.

4562
05:32:37,900 --> 05:32:38,920
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: I think I have a photo.

4563
05:32:39,340 --> 05:32:39,860
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Ayan po.

4564
05:32:40,180 --> 05:32:41,660
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Nagtatanim po yung mga mommies.

4565
05:32:42,580 --> 05:32:44,900
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: And moving forward, yan po yung tinanim nila.

4566
05:32:45,280 --> 05:32:47,780
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: This is not planting lang.

4567
05:32:48,060 --> 05:32:51,020
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: This is on the concept of the first 1,000 days.

4568
05:32:51,020 --> 05:32:53,900
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: This is a collab po between the DOH.

4569
05:32:53,900 --> 05:32:56,560
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: At the DA and the DOLE.

4570
05:32:56,840 --> 05:32:59,320
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: So, the DOLE po yung nagbabayad.

4571
05:32:59,640 --> 05:33:02,700
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: The DOH po, you need to learn about breastfeeding.

4572
05:33:03,100 --> 05:33:04,860
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Tapos yung DA po, food security.

4573
05:33:05,120 --> 05:33:07,340
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: So, ang nagmamonitor naman po doon.

4574
05:33:07,420 --> 05:33:10,820
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Nakikita naman po pag wala kayong gulay na ma-produce, talagang may problema.

4575
05:33:11,520 --> 05:33:15,100
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: And then lastly, I also wanted to share yung coastal clean up po namin.

4576
05:33:15,880 --> 05:33:19,740
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Ito po yung naglinis ng estero sa lugar po namin.

4577
05:33:20,300 --> 05:33:23,120
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: This is again, a form of natural flood control.

4578
05:33:23,120 --> 05:33:29,120
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Tapos ang nagmonitor naman po yung estero rangers po ng DNR.

4579
05:33:29,960 --> 05:33:31,060
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: So, nabenta po sila.

4580
05:33:31,500 --> 05:33:33,020
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: So, there has been monitoring.

4581
05:33:33,180 --> 05:33:37,180
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: So, I would like to personally thank Secretary for your assistance po.

4582
05:33:37,980 --> 05:33:40,300
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: And lastly, maraming salamat.

4583
05:33:40,520 --> 05:33:44,920
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: So, maybe we could have a Tupad Conference para i-award nyo po yung pinaka-innovative.

4584
05:33:45,620 --> 05:33:49,020
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Hindi, yung natutuwa po kayo so that others could learn po also.

4585
05:33:50,960 --> 05:33:52,440
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: And kailangan po talaga.

4586
05:33:53,120 --> 05:33:58,040
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Malaman natin kung ano yung magaganda and that we could emulate them parang ganun po.

4587
05:33:58,820 --> 05:34:02,060
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: So, magra-round 2 na lang po ako para sa test.

4588
05:34:02,160 --> 05:34:03,780
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Babalik pa ako para sa inyo.

4589
05:34:05,280 --> 05:34:06,920
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: So, thank you so much po.

4590
05:34:07,180 --> 05:34:09,180
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: I would like to commend our Secretary.

4591
05:34:09,440 --> 05:34:11,780
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: And of course, he cannot do it naman po by himself.

4592
05:34:11,780 --> 05:34:19,780
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: So, I would like to publicly thank R.D. Geraldine Tolentino at yung DOLE team namin na napakasipag po talaga.

4593
05:34:21,500 --> 05:34:21,940
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Panlilio.

4594
05:34:22,000 --> 05:34:22,600
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Yes, sorry.

4595
05:34:22,600 --> 05:34:23,300
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Panlilio.

4596
05:34:23,400 --> 05:34:30,880
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Ma'am Geraldine Panlilio, our Region 3 po na tumulong po sa amin to find innovative ways to do Tupad.

4597
05:34:31,280 --> 05:34:33,600
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: And baka naman you might consider also rebranding.

4598
05:34:35,140 --> 05:34:40,940
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Kasi, hindi kasi when people, because of the bad connotation that happened po before,

4599
05:34:41,080 --> 05:34:46,500
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: which I know you have been working very hard for para po mapalitan yung concept nga po ng ayuda.

4600
05:34:47,100 --> 05:34:49,320
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: You might think of rebranding the Tupad.

4601
05:34:49,320 --> 05:34:52,460
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Kasi once people see the Tupad, nagagalit po yung iba.

4602
05:34:52,600 --> 05:34:53,720
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Kasi hindi sila pinili.

4603
05:34:54,720 --> 05:34:55,780
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Hindi, ganun talaga eh.

4604
05:34:55,880 --> 05:34:58,820
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: So, you may consider that also.

4605
05:34:59,360 --> 05:35:06,560
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: So, yung sa amin, yung first 1,000 days, yung mga mamis po doon, yun ang mga nanganak from 0 to 6 months pa lamang.

4606
05:35:06,940 --> 05:35:11,840
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: So, we are, nagmimenos din po kami sa child malnutrition.

4607
05:35:12,380 --> 05:35:13,920
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: So, marami hong nagtatanong sa akin,

4608
05:35:14,180 --> 05:35:15,800
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Ma'am, bakit hindi kami napili?

4609
05:35:16,120 --> 05:35:17,440
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: So, sabi ko, mga nakamuna.

4610
05:35:17,440 --> 05:35:20,200
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Hindi, kinuha ko talaga lahat na nanganak.

4611
05:35:20,480 --> 05:35:22,440
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: So, ngayon, marami naman hong nagpapabunti.

4612
05:35:22,600 --> 05:35:25,960
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: So, unfortunately, nangyayari din po yun.

4613
05:35:26,920 --> 05:35:31,280
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: So, thank you so much, Sec, and sa Dole family.

4614
05:35:31,440 --> 05:35:32,200
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Thank you so much.

4615
05:35:32,500 --> 05:35:35,360
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: And sana po, mas marami pa po tayong matulungan.

4616
05:35:35,880 --> 05:35:38,700
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: And tama po kayo, we need to be flexible to the times din po.

4617
05:35:38,780 --> 05:35:40,620
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Kasi ang dami pong nangyayaring disasters.

4618
05:35:41,440 --> 05:35:42,780
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: So, maraming salamat po.

4619
05:35:42,980 --> 05:35:45,040
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: And more power po sa Dole.

4620
05:35:45,580 --> 05:35:47,060
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: And babalik po ako for the test.

4621
05:35:47,540 --> 05:35:48,560
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Thank you so much.

4622
05:35:49,440 --> 05:35:51,300
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Thank you, Rep. Anna York.

4623
05:35:52,600 --> 05:35:54,200
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Ngayon, may president na rin tayo.

4624
05:35:54,340 --> 05:35:55,600
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Hindi ko pa nagagawa yun yung ano.

4625
05:35:56,400 --> 05:35:57,300
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Kaya lang, mabuntis muna.

4626
05:35:59,660 --> 05:36:00,660
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Before I continue,

4627
05:36:01,300 --> 05:36:05,520
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Before I continue, I'd like to, the chair wishes to acknowledge Rep. Renee Louise Co.

4628
05:36:06,160 --> 05:36:08,180
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: And we move along to the minority.

4629
05:36:09,400 --> 05:36:12,680
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: I may call on to Rep. Iris Montes.

4630
05:36:13,160 --> 05:36:14,220
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Thank you, Mr. Chair.

4631
05:36:14,720 --> 05:36:16,700
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Magandang hapon po sa ating lahat.

4632
05:36:16,920 --> 05:36:21,700
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: The concern raised by Congresswoman Anna York Bondok is actually

4633
05:36:22,600 --> 05:36:23,960
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: one of my concerns also.

4634
05:36:24,100 --> 05:36:27,680
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: In fact, last budget hearing, I already raised that to the Dole.

4635
05:36:27,680 --> 05:36:31,780
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: And I am glad, ibida ko na lang po sa Region 4A,

4636
05:36:32,280 --> 05:36:35,860
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: meron ng mga pagbabagong ginawa sa TUPAD.

4637
05:36:36,200 --> 05:36:41,180
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: And like Congresswoman Anna York, meron din po sa amin yung gulayan.

4638
05:36:41,440 --> 05:36:46,680
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: We do that and we are piloting the 31 days po na TUPAD program.

4639
05:36:47,020 --> 05:36:50,720
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Hindi lang po 7 days, 10 days, kundi 31 days.

4640
05:36:51,060 --> 05:36:52,180
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Para to ensure,

4641
05:36:52,180 --> 05:36:55,560
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: na yung inumpisahan, makikita yung resulta at the end.

4642
05:36:55,900 --> 05:37:00,140
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: And they committed na tatapusin, kahit wala na po silang sweldo,

4643
05:37:00,460 --> 05:37:03,340
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: yung aming mga kababaihan, na ipagpapatuloy po

4644
05:37:03,340 --> 05:37:06,740
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: yung community gardening and planting po nila.

4645
05:37:07,080 --> 05:37:09,500
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: We also did coastal cleanup.

4646
05:37:10,100 --> 05:37:16,940
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: And ngayon po sa Region 4A, meron po silang geo-tagging na po ng TUPAD.

4647
05:37:16,940 --> 05:37:21,420
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So nakikita in real time kung mga nagtatrabaho po ba yung mga,

4648
05:37:22,180 --> 05:37:24,500
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: yung sa TUPAD.

4649
05:37:24,660 --> 05:37:28,160
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Pero may mga challenges kasi there are areas na wala pong signal.

4650
05:37:28,600 --> 05:37:30,160
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So walang geo-tagging.

4651
05:37:30,340 --> 05:37:37,440
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: But I commend the DOLE for listening na magkaroon ng pagbabago at reform

4652
05:37:37,440 --> 05:37:39,820
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: sa pag-implement ng TUPAD.

4653
05:37:40,480 --> 05:37:45,700
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Moving on po, yung question ko po talagang ito.

4654
05:37:46,820 --> 05:37:51,580
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: It's often said that our human resource, our people,

4655
05:37:51,580 --> 05:37:54,380
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: is our most important human resource.

4656
05:37:54,760 --> 05:37:59,000
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: But today, we are confronted po with a sad news.

4657
05:37:59,280 --> 05:38:01,740
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: A few hours ago, it's all over the news,

4658
05:38:02,280 --> 05:38:07,720
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: that our unemployment for July has risen to 6% from 4.9,

4659
05:38:08,020 --> 05:38:12,260
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: translating to about 314 Filipinos who are out of jobs.

4660
05:38:13,960 --> 05:38:17,120
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: 3 million Filipinos.

4661
05:38:18,120 --> 05:38:21,120
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Our labor force participation rate has also,

4662
05:38:21,580 --> 05:38:25,740
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: has also dipped to 63.6 from 65.

4663
05:38:26,520 --> 05:38:29,540
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: And then we have a rising unemployment rate.

4664
05:38:30,240 --> 05:38:35,840
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So we are in a very trying times and challenging times.

4665
05:38:36,020 --> 05:38:36,740
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So I understand.

4666
05:38:37,300 --> 05:38:47,560
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Even the DEPDEP admitted that we have to scale up our efforts

4667
05:38:47,560 --> 05:38:50,960
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: to create more jobs and quality jobs at that.

4668
05:38:51,580 --> 05:38:56,280
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: But the DOLE has also said that it will intensify its efforts.

4669
05:38:56,680 --> 05:39:01,400
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Given po, Mr. Secretary, ng budget na meron tayo,

4670
05:39:01,860 --> 05:39:05,980
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: paano po natin actually may intensify yung efforts natin?

4671
05:39:06,120 --> 05:39:08,720
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Especially po, sa figure na ito po yata,

4672
05:39:09,100 --> 05:39:11,760
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: yung mga youth dyan, yung mga bagong graduates,

4673
05:39:12,200 --> 05:39:15,120
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: hindi daw nagkaroon ng pagkakataon na makasali

4674
05:39:15,120 --> 05:39:19,300
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: kasi sa labor force, kasi walang available na trabaho.

4675
05:39:19,300 --> 05:39:20,360
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So how do we plan?

4676
05:39:20,700 --> 05:39:21,520
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Given our budget,

4677
05:39:21,520 --> 05:39:24,540
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: how do we scale up employment, especially for the youth?

4678
05:39:25,400 --> 05:39:26,300
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Tama po kayo, Your Honor.

4679
05:39:26,600 --> 05:39:33,800
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Medyo hindi maganda yung lumabas ngayon na labor force survey.

4680
05:39:35,420 --> 05:39:36,060
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Tumaas.

4681
05:39:36,580 --> 05:39:42,220
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Nag-decline yung employment rate from 94% to 94.7% in July.

4682
05:39:42,820 --> 05:39:46,340
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Unemployment rate increased to 6% from 5.3.

4683
05:39:46,340 --> 05:39:51,340
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: So yung unemployed persons rose from 551,000 year-on-year

4684
05:39:51,520 --> 05:39:56,100
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: from 2.59 million to 3.14 million.

4685
05:39:56,440 --> 05:39:58,020
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Ito po, mga katabi ko, Your Honor,

4686
05:39:58,700 --> 05:40:03,560
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: mamaya siguro para makasagot na si Tesla Secretary,

4687
05:40:03,700 --> 05:40:08,100
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: mapapaliwanag niya yung ginagawa po doon sa Tesla Skills Passport

4688
05:40:08,100 --> 05:40:10,380
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: na inulunsad ngayong taon na to.

4689
05:40:10,940 --> 05:40:14,680
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Ganon din po yung aming nilagdaan, nakaalaman tungo sa kabuhayan.

4690
05:40:15,000 --> 05:40:16,460
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Ang tinutukoy ko po rito,

4691
05:40:17,560 --> 05:40:19,660
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: sinasabi nyo kasi, bumaba yung amin.

4692
05:40:20,120 --> 05:40:21,160
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Bumaba rin yung kanila.

4693
05:40:21,520 --> 05:40:22,920
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Pero pag kami nagsanib po,

4694
05:40:23,980 --> 05:40:30,200
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: merong kaukulang risulta siguro na pwedeng asahan yung Dole-Tesda convergence.

4695
05:40:30,420 --> 05:40:34,060
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: So papaliwanag po yan ni Secretary Kiko mamaya.

4696
05:40:34,060 --> 05:40:44,300
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: But let me ask Usec Torres to give a more detailed quantified analysis

4697
05:40:44,300 --> 05:40:51,340
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: of what really came out of that LFS, that survey today.

4698
05:40:51,520 --> 05:40:54,860
DOLE Undersecretary Carmela I. Torres: Maraming salamat po, Secretary, Your Honor.

4699
05:40:55,360 --> 05:40:57,040
DOLE Undersecretary Carmela I. Torres: Magandang hapon po sa inyong lahat.

4700
05:40:57,940 --> 05:41:00,460
DOLE Undersecretary Carmela I. Torres: Napaka-importante pong question kasi nga,

4701
05:41:00,780 --> 05:41:03,840
DOLE Undersecretary Carmela I. Torres: we're concerned na tumaas yung ating unemployment rate.

4702
05:41:04,340 --> 05:41:08,960
DOLE Undersecretary Carmela I. Torres: At marami pong causes at unang-una nga nabanggit po nyo yung ating kabataan.

4703
05:41:09,400 --> 05:41:13,560
DOLE Undersecretary Carmela I. Torres: Ang nangyari po ay na-increase yung new entrance sa labor market.

4704
05:41:14,260 --> 05:41:17,500
DOLE Undersecretary Carmela I. Torres: And if you recall, yung ating gross domestic product,

4705
05:41:17,500 --> 05:41:20,500
DOLE Undersecretary Carmela I. Torres: nag-grow lang ang economy sa 2.3%.

4706
05:41:21,520 --> 05:41:25,300
DOLE Undersecretary Carmela I. Torres: So dahil mabagal yung growth, mabagal din yung industry,

4707
05:41:25,480 --> 05:41:29,040
DOLE Undersecretary Carmela I. Torres: hindi po nakakatch up yung ating employment.

4708
05:41:29,760 --> 05:41:31,060
DOLE Undersecretary Carmela I. Torres: So bumagal din.

4709
05:41:31,240 --> 05:41:35,540
DOLE Undersecretary Carmela I. Torres: Kaya dumami po yung unemployed na youth.

4710
05:41:36,120 --> 05:41:39,600
DOLE Undersecretary Carmela I. Torres: Kaya po napaka-importante na tingnan po natin to,

4711
05:41:39,760 --> 05:41:42,540
DOLE Undersecretary Carmela I. Torres: kung sino yung mga youth, saan sila located,

4712
05:41:43,140 --> 05:41:45,300
DOLE Undersecretary Carmela I. Torres: at kung saan malaki yung job losses.

4713
05:41:45,300 --> 05:41:50,600
DOLE Undersecretary Carmela I. Torres: Na-identify po namin yung mga job losses kasama dyan po ang agriculture,

4714
05:41:50,860 --> 05:41:51,400
DOLE Undersecretary Carmela I. Torres: manufacturing.

4715
05:41:51,520 --> 05:41:55,960
DOLE Undersecretary Carmela I. Torres: Kung saan natin dapat i-enhance yung employment.

4716
05:41:56,540 --> 05:41:59,700
DOLE Undersecretary Carmela I. Torres: Saka yung ating mga youth para sa ating, ano,

4717
05:41:59,880 --> 05:42:02,320
DOLE Undersecretary Carmela I. Torres: to find out kung saan sila pwede ma-employ.

4718
05:42:02,900 --> 05:42:06,920
DOLE Undersecretary Carmela I. Torres: I-link po yung ating employment, school to employment transition,

4719
05:42:07,060 --> 05:42:10,260
DOLE Undersecretary Carmela I. Torres: yung po yung in-emphasize nga po ni Secretary Tolentino,

4720
05:42:10,660 --> 05:42:15,100
DOLE Undersecretary Carmela I. Torres: na-enhance po natin yung transition from school to work ng ating mga kabataan.

4721
05:42:15,500 --> 05:42:20,560
DOLE Undersecretary Carmela I. Torres: Dumami po kasi yung ating graduates, kaya talagang kailangan natin i-catch up yan.

4722
05:42:20,560 --> 05:42:24,380
DOLE Undersecretary Carmela I. Torres: At ang isa pong ating kailangang i-intensify,

4723
05:42:24,980 --> 05:42:27,020
DOLE Undersecretary Carmela I. Torres: yung ating youth employability program.

4724
05:42:27,260 --> 05:42:34,160
DOLE Undersecretary Carmela I. Torres: Nabanggit ko na po earlier, napaka-useful yung ating government internship program,

4725
05:42:34,880 --> 05:42:42,440
DOLE Undersecretary Carmela I. Torres: na kung saan binibigyan natin pagkakataon yung ating mga youth na ma-employ sa ating government service

4726
05:42:42,440 --> 05:42:45,040
DOLE Undersecretary Carmela I. Torres: and to have careers in government service,

4727
05:42:45,040 --> 05:42:49,060
DOLE Undersecretary Carmela I. Torres: yung ating special program for the employment of students,

4728
05:42:49,180 --> 05:42:50,480
DOLE Undersecretary Carmela I. Torres: at saka po yung ating jobs.

4729
05:42:50,560 --> 05:42:54,620
DOLE Undersecretary Carmela I. Torres: At yung ating job start na napaka-famous po sa ating mga mga kabataan.

4730
05:42:55,480 --> 05:43:01,960
DOLE Undersecretary Carmela I. Torres: Yung isa po ay yung ating i-intensify yung ating support through our employment facilitation

4731
05:43:01,960 --> 05:43:07,000
DOLE Undersecretary Carmela I. Torres: kasi kailangan silang mag-guide kung saan talaga yung employment and vacancies.

4732
05:43:07,220 --> 05:43:13,580
DOLE Undersecretary Carmela I. Torres: Maraming po tayong occupations na hard to fill and emerging at kailangan natin i-guide sila.

4733
05:43:13,580 --> 05:43:20,300
DOLE Undersecretary Carmela I. Torres: Dun po sa ating two frameworks, existing frameworks ay Trabajo Para sa Bayan Plan,

4734
05:43:20,560 --> 05:43:21,980
DOLE Undersecretary Carmela I. Torres: and labor and employment plan.

4735
05:43:22,060 --> 05:43:30,580
DOLE Undersecretary Carmela I. Torres: Naka-identify po tayo ng mga key growth centers nationwide at kung saan malaki yung employment

4736
05:43:30,580 --> 05:43:38,440
DOLE Undersecretary Carmela I. Torres: at dun po natin kailangan i-guide from education, our one education which is DepEd, TESDA, and CHED

4737
05:43:38,440 --> 05:43:41,840
DOLE Undersecretary Carmela I. Torres: to work together to guide them for employment.

4738
05:43:41,840 --> 05:43:44,220
DOLE Undersecretary Carmela I. Torres: So yun po yung ating ginagawa sa DOLE.

4739
05:43:44,640 --> 05:43:46,840
DOLE Undersecretary Carmela I. Torres: Si Sec. Tolentino po will...

4740
05:43:47,480 --> 05:43:49,840
DOLE Undersecretary Carmela I. Torres: Ay, ay, ay, Sec. Benitez will...

4741
05:43:50,560 --> 05:43:57,160
DOLE Undersecretary Carmela I. Torres: Give you details on kailangan po rin natin yung upskilling and reskilling and also our internship apprenticeship program.

4742
05:43:58,460 --> 05:43:58,920
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: Sige po.

4743
05:43:59,920 --> 05:44:06,380
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: Siguro unahin ko na lang that I will echo you Sec. Torres' position or statement

4744
05:44:06,380 --> 05:44:13,500
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: that the slowdown in the macroeconomic of the country has also made itself felt in the employment figures.

4745
05:44:13,740 --> 05:44:18,620
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: And so what it really will require is to intensify two things.

4746
05:44:18,840 --> 05:44:20,500
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: Actually three things na na-mention na rin.

4747
05:44:20,560 --> 05:44:27,860
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: The first is obviously matching the job openings to the people that might be looking for a job.

4748
05:44:27,860 --> 05:44:37,820
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: Sa area-based demand-driven po namin, malinaw po na meron pong more job openings, no?

4749
05:44:38,320 --> 05:44:47,260
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: In fact, then we have unemployed Filipinos, which really suggests that the job openings that DOLE itself actually puts together

4750
05:44:47,260 --> 05:44:50,140
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: in the peso, in the public employment service offices,

4751
05:44:50,560 --> 05:44:55,440
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: that information doesn't reach the right people who might be the right fit for those jobs.

4752
05:44:55,840 --> 05:45:00,140
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: So anything that we can do to improve that and intensify

4753
05:45:00,140 --> 05:45:07,440
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: that link, the faster we can address unemployment, at least in terms of employment per se.

4754
05:45:07,820 --> 05:45:17,500
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: The second is, of course, nabanggit rin ni Yusek Torres, is the job skills mismatching with regards to DepEd, TESDA, and CHED

4755
05:45:17,500 --> 05:45:24,560
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: to make sure that our youth actually have the right skills for the kind of jobs that are available to them.

4756
05:45:24,560 --> 05:45:36,360
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: So, nandyan nga ang JobStart, meron pong fieldjobs.net, at ang nabanggit po ni Secretary Tolentino kanina is that TESDA put together the skills passport

4757
05:45:36,360 --> 05:45:48,480
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: precisely to provide a digital platform to help create these linkages and address information asymmetry para at least hindi po information ang kulang.

4758
05:45:48,480 --> 05:45:53,360
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: So that JobStart, fieldjobs.net, and so on.

4759
05:45:53,720 --> 05:45:54,480
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: Our...

4760
05:45:54,560 --> 05:46:02,560
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: At the least, TVET graduates can have access online in real time to the job openings that are available.

4761
05:46:03,500 --> 05:46:10,900
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: These are all being designed to make sure that our supply and our demand meet together.

4762
05:46:10,900 --> 05:46:23,100
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: So, ang ano na lang dyan, ma'am, is how effectively, how intensively, no, both Dole and TESDA can in fact roll out this program with the kind of urgency that we need.

4763
05:46:23,720 --> 05:46:24,340
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: Sana naman po.

4764
05:46:24,560 --> 05:46:34,680
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: The other piece that should be clear is that we need to make sure that demand side is commensurate.

4765
05:46:34,920 --> 05:46:43,100
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: So, Bureau of Investment naman po yan because we need to make sure that industry opens up and has as much job openings that are of decent work

4766
05:46:43,100 --> 05:46:54,540
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: and of the decent scale of quality of salaries and so on, that again, bahagi po yan sa macroeconomic slowdown ng...

4767
05:46:54,540 --> 05:46:55,260
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: ng country.

4768
05:46:55,740 --> 05:47:04,660
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: So, kanina, nagtanong po si kong Robert tungkol po sa area-based demand-driven approach ng prioritization ng TESDA.

4769
05:47:05,240 --> 05:47:15,880
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: No, what we try to do is to prioritize at least government funds to those sectors that have the most demand or most emerging job openings.

4770
05:47:15,880 --> 05:47:23,880
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: So, nandyan po, kagaya ng kanina pang pinag-uusapan ng ICT, ang AI, nandyan po ang actually maritime tourism and services.

4771
05:47:24,540 --> 05:47:25,560
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: No, industry.

4772
05:47:26,140 --> 05:47:29,940
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: Nandyan po ang semiconductors and advanced manufacturing.

4773
05:47:30,380 --> 05:47:37,240
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: All of these are sectors that are being prioritized because we know that the jobs are actually available

4774
05:47:37,240 --> 05:47:43,600
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: and we need to make sure that our workforce is appropriately skilled for the jobs that actually exist.

4775
05:47:45,690 --> 05:47:46,910
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Maraming salamat po.

4776
05:47:47,450 --> 05:47:54,410
